{
  "citations": [
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 9,
      "quote": "| A-ST50-VIB-HH | ST50 Conveyor: vibration high-high | `vibration_rms_mms` above 7.1 mm/s; trip: the station stops |"
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 15,
      "quote": "Drive-end bearing vibration (`vibration_rms_mms`) rises out of its normal range of 0.8 to 2.8 mm/s, slowly at first and then faster. The one-second RMS trend carries a ripple at the pulley rotation frequency (about 0.255 Hz at 12 m/min, one turn every 3.9 s). Bearing temperature (`bearing_temp_c`) follows some minutes later; motor current rises slightly and chain speed sags."
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 15,
      "quote": "Vibration that grows in an accelerating curve, with a ripple at the pulley rotation frequency and a delayed rise in bearing temperature, indicates a drive-end bearing defect."
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 15,
      "quote": "| `vibration_rms_mms` above 2.8 mm/s and accelerating, ripple at 1x pulley rotation | Drive-end bearing defect (race or rolling element damage) | Spectrum of a high-rate snapshot; listen with a stethoscope; check the grease condition | Plan a bearing replacement; reduce speed only under change control; replace at the next stop |"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "citations": [
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 16,
      "quote": "A reading that jumps beyond a trip limit for one to three seconds and then returns, with no change in related tags before or after, is a measurement spike; reset, record it and keep the station running."
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 16,
      "quote": "A real process change moves more than one signal; a single tag that trends steadily while every physically related tag stays normal points to the instrument, not the process."
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 17,
      "quote": "| Station stopped on a high-high or low-low trip after a one- to three-second excursion | Measurement spike (electrical noise, loose shield, vibration on the cable) | Check the trend either side of the trip; check related tags; inspect cable shield and gland | Reset and restart; if spikes repeat, re-terminate the shield and re-route the cable away from power cables |"
    },
    {
      "doc": "conveyor_drive",
      "page": 14,
      "quote": "Before performing physical adjustments or component replacements, inspect instrument cabling and sensor mountings to rule out faulty sensor data."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "citations": [
    {
      "doc": "sealer_pump",
      "page": 9,
      "quote": "| A-ST40-BLOCKED | ST40 Sealer: station blocked (outfeed full) | Consequence of a slow or stopped station downstream; not a fault at this station |"
    },
    {
      "doc": "sealer_pump",
      "page": 13,
      "quote": "| Stations downstream starved and stations upstream blocked after a shift start | A slower cycle at one station propagating along the line | Find the first station whose cycle time changed; downstream starvation and upstream blocking are consequences | Correct the parameter at the first station only |"
    }
  ]
}
